-- pops .output on its own -- and THEN fails. Before the fix, the processor's
-- Syntax handler popped a second time, .output fell to .NIL, and the handler
-- died on its first Say (97.1), swallowing this division-by-zero entirely:
-- the client got a pristine 404 and error.log recorded only the secondary
-- 97.1. After the fix the handler asks the stack (current isA OutputStream)
-- before popping, sees the buffer is already gone, does NOT pop, and its
-- error page -- naming THIS failure -- reaches the client and the log.
